 "method": "Design invariant under Z2^2 x Z3 (two orbits of 12 bowlers). Z2^2 fixes every oil block: each week is either fixed by all of Z2^2 or is one of a pair {W, tW} with W fixed by one involution, so a week's couples are whole Z2^2-classes (78 classes) and the design is an exact cover of classes by 380,000 candidate weeks/week-pairs. Z3 cycles the three 6-week blocks and fixes each week of the 5-week block; an exhaustive class-cover DFS (asearch.c) found block 1 given the 5-week block. Z3 also rotates the lane pairs in two tracks of three (lanes_eq.c, annealing over block 1's group orders and 18 choices per week of block 4). 4 clash-free blocks 6+6+6+5 (the lower bound); the disjoint leaves force prefix spread <= 2 for any week order; positions by de Werra (positions.assign)."
